066681.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/former-openai-engineer-accused-of-planting-office-bug-had-ties-with-saudi-royal-family-us-prosecutors/articleshow/135066681.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/former-openai-engineer-accused-of-planting-office-bug-had-ties-with-saudi-royal-family-us-prosecutors/articleshow/135066681.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T15:10:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135066927,imgsize-878081.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Ken Schreiber, retired pilot who donated $400,000 to save Neil Armstrong's childhood home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135064878.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ken Schreiber has made a generous donation of $400,000 with the aim of preserving Neil Armstrong's childhood home, highlighting its important place in history. The Auglaize County Historical Society plans to restore the house to its original 1940s charm, inspired by Schreiber's deep admiration for Armstrong. Scheduled for public tours by 2030, this initiative ensures that future generations can appreciate the legacy of the first man on the moon.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-was-9-when-neil-armstrong-walked-on-the-moon-57-years-later-retired-pilot-ken-schreiber-has-spent-400000-to-help-preserve-the-astronauts-boyhood-home-and-open-it-to-visitors/articleshow/135064878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-was-9-when-neil-armstrong-walked-on-the-moon-57-years-later-retired-pilot-ken-schreiber-has-spent-400000-to-help-preserve-the-astronauts-boyhood-home-and-open-it-to-visitors/articleshow/135064878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T15:09:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135065053,imgsize-1120316.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US dealer’s $14,000 gold egg turns out to be lost Fabergé treasure worth $33M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135064798.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-us-scrap-metal-dealer-paid-about-14000-for-a-gold-egg-at-an-antiques-market-hoping-to-melt-it-for-profit-years-later-it-was-identified-as-a-lost-imperial-faberg-treasure-reportedly-worth-up-to-33-million/articleshow/135064798.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-us-scrap-metal-dealer-paid-about-14000-for-a-gold-egg-at-an-antiques-market-hoping-to-melt-it-for-profit-years-later-it-was-identified-as-a-lost-imperial-faberg-treasure-reportedly-worth-up-to-33-million/articleshow/135064798.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T14:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135064859,imgsize-775026.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US couple pays $4,995 for century-old fridge, spends another $2,000 getting it to work]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135063888.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan couple bought a 116-year-old refrigerator for $4,995 on Facebook Marketplace, but getting the massive appliance into their farmhouse proved difficult. Weighing over 1,000 pounds, it required seven weeks of preparation, specialist movers, reinforced floors and additional expenses. Despite the challenges, the couple restored it to working condition and made it a central part of their family home.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-couple-bought-a-116-year-old-1000-pound-refrigerator-for-4995-on-facebook-marketplace-after-seven-weeks-a-1200-move-and-reinforced-floors-the-7-foot-wide-appliance-became-the-center-of-their-kitchen/articleshow/135063888.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-couple-bought-a-116-year-old-1000-pound-refrigerator-for-4995-on-facebook-marketplace-after-seven-weeks-a-1200-move-and-reinforced-floors-the-7-foot-wide-appliance-became-the-center-of-their-kitchen/articleshow/135063888.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T14:58:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135064808,imgsize-160178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: Burning e-bikes turned into bonfires as France reels from violent protests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135064827.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[France witnessed a violent weekend as protests over rising living costs and underfunded public services escalated into riots and looting. Burning e-bikes, torched vehicles and smoke-filled streets marked the unrest in Paris and other cities. Hundreds of shared bikes and scooters were damaged, causing an estimated €400,000 in losses to one operator. Authorities arrested around 2,400 people and are tightening security to prevent further violence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/watch-burning-e-bikes-turned-into-bonfires-as-france-reels-from-violent-protests/articleshow/135064827.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/watch-burning-e-bikes-turned-into-bonfires-as-france-reels-from-violent-protests/articleshow/135064827.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T14:16:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135065567,imgsize-1910105.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1880s Rhode Island social club hits market at $9.75 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135063908.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Reading Room, an iconic establishment in Narragansett, has hit the market, presenting a unique opportunity for discerning buyers. This beautifully restored five-bedroom residence retains its historic charm after significant renovations in 2010. With a current asking price of $9.75 million, it boasts breathtaking views and generous outdoor areas, making it an exceptional find for those seeking a distinctive home.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/iconic-1880s-rhode-island-waterfront-social-club-is-being-offered-for-the-first-time-in-50-years-after-a-1-2-million-price-cut-the-historic-five-bedroom-property-now-asks-9-75-million/articleshow/135063908.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/iconic-1880s-rhode-island-waterfront-social-club-is-being-offered-for-the-first-time-in-50-years-after-a-1-2-million-price-cut-the-historic-five-bedroom-property-now-asks-9-75-million/articleshow/135063908.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T13:57:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135064265,imgsize-160490.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nashville held a developer's permit for years over a future road; appeals court revives lawsuit]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135063840.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A federal appeals court has reinstated the lawsuit of SW Nashville EB Owner, LLC against the city of Nashville regarding a stalled building permit. The developer faced an indefinite delay on their application, purportedly linked to prospective road developments, resulting in losses exceeding $8.2 million while the property remained undeveloped. The court's decision enables the developer's claims to progress to judicial review, potentially influencing other property owners experiencing similar challenges.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-a-nashville-developer-bought-a-vacant-lot-but-the-city-held-its-building-permit-for-four-years-while-weighing-a-future-road-a-federal-appeals-court-has-now-revived-its-lawsuit-over-the-freeze/articleshow/135063840.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-a-nashville-developer-bought-a-vacant-lot-but-the-city-held-its-building-permit-for-four-years-while-weighing-a-future-road-a-federal-appeals-court-has-now-revived-its-lawsuit-over-the-freeze/articleshow/135063840.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135063934,imgsize-1762885.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kentucky sinks 1,700 discarded Christmas trees in a lake to create homes for fish]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135063031.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kentucky collected around 5,000 discarded Christmas trees in 2026 to restore underwater habitats in its ageing lakes. As part of the state's 'Christmas for the Fishes' programme, approximately 1,700 trees were submerged in Boltz Lake alone. The trees provide shelter and feeding areas for fish, replacing natural structures that have decayed over time. The initiative also helps improve recreational fishing opportunities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/kentucky-collected-about-5000-discarded-christmas-trees-in-2026-instead-of-sending-them-to-landfills-officials-sank-1700-in-a-single-lake-to-replace-lost-underwater-shelter-for-fish/articleshow/135063031.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/kentucky-collected-about-5000-discarded-christmas-trees-in-2026-instead-of-sending-them-to-landfills-officials-sank-1700-in-a-single-lake-to-replace-lost-underwater-shelter-for-fish/articleshow/135063031.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135063734,imgsize-242506.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rihanna’s Fenty Beauty faces potential sale of its 50% stake after 2017 launch]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135064272.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/rihanna-launched-fenty-beauty-in-2017-with-a-40-shade-foundation-range-years-later-its-co-owner-began-exploring-a-sale-of-its-50-stake/articleshow/135064272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/rihanna-launched-fenty-beauty-in-2017-with-a-40-shade-foundation-range-years-later-its-co-owner-began-exploring-a-sale-of-its-50-stake/articleshow/135064272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135064344,imgsize-777237.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kylie Jenner launched lip kit in 2015; Coty bought 51% for $600 million in 2019]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135063223.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kylie-jenner-launched-a-lip-kit-in-2015-and-built-a-global-cosmetics-brand-coty-agreed-to-pay-600-million-for-a-51-stake-in-2019/articleshow/135063223.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kylie-jenner-launched-a-lip-kit-in-2015-and-built-a-global-cosmetics-brand-coty-agreed-to-pay-600-million-for-a-51-stake-in-2019/articleshow/135063223.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T15:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135063372,imgsize-642388.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After 11 road accidents, English villagers knit fake police officers to slow down drivers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135062416.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Villagers in Fillongley, England, spent four months knitting life-sized traffic officers, fake speed cameras and roadside figures after 11 accidents were recorded at a junction over four years. Installed on October 13, the handmade displays have reportedly prompted some drivers to slow down. However, one knitted RAF officer has apparently been stolen, while residents continue to await permanent road safety improvements.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/after-11-road-accidents-in-four-years-villagers-in-england-spent-four-months-knitting-life-sized-police-officers-and-fake-speed-cameras-their-handmade-decoys-are-now-making-some-drivers-hit-the-brakes/articleshow/135062416.cms]]></link><g