ance-will-donate-the-bulk-of-his-wealth-to-philanthropy/articleshow/135062820.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-space-industry-entrepreneur-made-his-first-million-at-27-but-plans-to-leave-his-children-only-an-eight-figure-inheritance-will-donate-the-bulk-of-his-wealth-to-philanthropy/articleshow/135062820.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T12:07:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135062950,imgsize-387492.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Five Years Of Pay-It-Forward Meals: JBJ Soul Kitchen marks milestone; more than half of guests are in need]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135042978.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[JBJ Soul Kitchen recently marked a significant milestone, celebrating five amazing years of service to the community. Founded by Jon Bon Jovi and his wife, the restaurant is committed to providing nourishing meals to students and local residents, regardless of financial means. With over 14,000 meals served, it actively combats food insecurity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/food-news/in-2020-jon-bon-jovi-and-his-wife-helped-open-a-restaurant-at-rutgersnewark-five-years-later-it-had-served-more-than-14000-meals-to-students-faculty-and-neighbours-regardless-of-ability-to-pay/articleshow/135042978.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/food-news/in-2020-jon-bon-jovi-and-his-wife-helped-open-a-restaurant-at-rutgersnewark-five-years-later-it-had-served-more-than-14000-meals-to-students-faculty-and-neighbours-regardless-of-ability-to-pay/articleshow/135042978.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T12:06:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135043010,imgsize-1435352.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[This Cold War missile silo in Kansas plunges 182 feet underground; its converted command centre is now a home listed for $1.6 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135061698.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A former missile silo in Kansas is listed for sale at $1.6 million after conversion. The property includes 2,500 square feet of livable space and a 182-foot silo. Originally built for military purposes, this site has modern amenities like high-speed internet. Future possibilities for the property include conference venues or residential condominiums. Buyers must consider the unique maintenance requirements of this underground structure before purchase.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-cold-war-missile-base-in-kansas-has-a-silo-plunging-182-feet-underground-owners-converted-its-neighbouring-command-centre-into-2500-square-feet-of-living-space-and-the-18-2-acre-site-now-asks-1-6-million/articleshow/135061698.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-cold-war-missile-base-in-kansas-has-a-silo-plunging-182-feet-underground-owners-converted-its-neighbouring-command-centre-into-2500-square-feet-of-living-space-and-the-18-2-acre-site-now-asks-1-6-million/articleshow/135061698.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T12:06:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135061788,imgsize-679782.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Goose Creek Substation Dispute: Judge raps Xcel over bad faith; appeal tests eminent domain limits]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135042353.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A contentious legal battle has arisen between Xcel Energy and the Dickey family regarding land essential for renewable energy initiatives. Xcel is contesting a recent ruling that restricts its eminent domain authority for an easement in Colorado. The conflict primarily revolves around fair compensation and proposed power line routes that impact the family's agricultural endeavors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-a-fourth-generation-colorado-farming-family-sold-90-acres-to-xcel-energy-for-585000-four-years-later-the-utility-sought-a-550-foot-easement-for-19000-but-a-judge-rejected-its-condemnation-bid/articleshow/135042353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-a-fourth-generation-colorado-farming-family-sold-90-acres-to-xcel-energy-for-585000-four-years-later-the-utility-sought-a-550-foot-easement-for-19000-but-a-judge-rejected-its-condemnation-bid/articleshow/135042353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T12:05:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135042552,imgsize-1269746.cms"/></item></channel></rss>